# ─── FRONTEND ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave this unset in almost every case:
#   - Local dev (npm run dev, port 5173) — api.js talks directly to localhost:8000.
#   - Deployed via this repo's docker-compose.yml — nginx reverse-proxies /api/*
#     to the backend container internally, so the app never needs a separate
#     backend URL at all (see nginx.conf).
#
# Only set this if the backend is reachable at its OWN separate public URL
# (i.e. you're not using the docker-compose/nginx setup as-is). Vite bakes this
# in at build time, so changing it requires a rebuild, not just a restart.
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-domain.example.com
